A routine lab renovation disturbs this totally uncatalogued legacy inventory.
一次例行的实验室翻修扰动了这批完全没有登记在册的遗留库存。

118
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:09,440
During the cleanup, workers who didn't have the proper mercury-specific PPE
在清理过程中，没有配备合适的汞专用个人防护装备的工作人员

119
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:14,560
were exposed to visible beads, and several ended up showing elevated urine mercury levels.
接触到了肉眼可见的汞珠，其中几人的尿汞水平升高。

120
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:19,840
It's a perfect illustration of how ignored, badly managed legacy inventory can just hide
这完美地说明了被忽视、管理不善的遗留库存如何能在设施中

121
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:24,960
in a facility like a ticking time bomb for decades, waiting for one routine event to trigger an exposure.
像定时炸弹一样潜伏几十年，只等一个例行事件来引发暴露。

122
00:08:25,520 --> 00:08:29,440
To stop those hidden risks from snowballing into full-blown disasters,
为了阻止这些隐藏的风险像滚雪球一样演变成全面的灾难，

123
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:34,880
your lab needs a rock-solid instant reporting culture that catches those tiny anomalies early.
你的实验室需要一种坚如磐石的事件报告文化，及早发现那些微小的异常。

124
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:36,240
So how do we build that?
那么我们如何建立这种文化呢？

125
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:41,040
Step one, you have to provide anonymous reporting channels alongside the named ones.
第一步，除了实名报告渠道，你还必须提供匿名报告渠道。

126
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:45,760
Step two, keep the time to feedback loop super short so people actually know their voices were
第二步，让反馈周期尽可能短，让人们真正知道自己的声音被

127
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:46,480
heard.
听到了。

128
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:49,440
Step three, visibly recognize and thank reporters.
第三步，公开地表彰和感谢报告人。

129
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:51,840
Zero blame, zero whistleblower stigma.
零指责，零举报污名。

130
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:55,600
And step four, systematically track every single corrective action
第四步，系统地跟踪每一项纠正措施，

131
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:57,360
right through to complete closure.
直到完全关闭。

132
00:08:57,360 --> 00:09:00,720
And speaking of corrective actions, we really need to define CAPA,
说到纠正措施，我们真的需要定义一下 CAPA，

133
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,720
Corrective and Preventive Action.
即纠正和预防措施。

134
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:04,960
The corrective piece stops the immediate bleeding,
纠正部分是立即止血，

135
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:08,560
while the preventative piece changes the system so it never happens again.
而预防部分则是改变系统，让问题永远不再发生。

136
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:10,160
But here is the major takeaway.
但这里有一个重要的启示。

137
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:13,440
A CAPA is entirely useless if you don't verify its effectiveness.
如果你不验证 CAPA 的有效性，它就完全没有用处。

138
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,800
If you just write up a new SOP and buy some shiny new equipment,
如果你只是写了一份新的 SOP，买了一些崭新的设备，

139
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:20,240
but you don't circle back six months later to verify that it actually worked,
却没有在六个月后回过头来验证它是否真的有效，

140
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,440
you aren't doing safety.
那你不是在做安全工作。

141
00:09:21,440 --> 00:09:22,960
You're literally just doing paperwork.
你只是在做文书工作。

142
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:27,040
I want to wrap up our explainer today with a pretty provocative question
在今天的讲解结束之际，我想提一个相当发人深省的问题，

143
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:29,760
about how we actually perceive safety metrics.
关于我们究竟如何看待安全指标。

144
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:32,480
Look around your own workspace for a second and ask yourself,
花点时间环顾一下你自己的工作场所，问问自己，

145
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:35,520
if your lab has a really high near-miss reporting rate,
如果你的实验室未遂事件报告率非常高，

146
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:38,320
meaning your team is constantly logging small mistakes,
也就是说你的团队在不断地记录小失误、

147
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:40,080
little spills and close calls,
小泄漏和险情，

148
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,400
does that mean your lab is inherently dangerous?
这是否意味着你的实验室本身就很危险？

149
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:45,440
Well, the answer is actually the exact opposite.
嗯，答案其实恰恰相反。

150
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:48,320
A lab with a high near-miss rate is almost always the lab
未遂事件报告率高的实验室，几乎总是那个

151
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:52,080
with an incredibly low recordable catastrophic incident rate.
可记录的灾难性事故率极低的实验室。

152
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:54,160
When a team feels genuinely safe enough
当一个团队真正感到足够安全，

153
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:57,120
to openly report their honest mistakes and near-misses,
能够公开报告自己的无心之失和未遂事件时，

154
00:09:57,120 --> 00:10:00,160
they're building this highly attuned, learning-focused environment
他们就在建立一个高度敏锐、注重学习的环境，

155
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:03,760
that catches the tiny patterns way before they ever result in a fatality.
能在微小的规律演变成致命事故之前就把它们发现。

156
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:06,320
A lab with zero near-miss reports?
一个零未遂事件报告的实验室？

157
00:10:06,320 --> 00:10:07,680
That's not a perfect lab.
那不是一个完美的实验室。

158
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:09,840
That's a silent lab, hiding its risks.
那是一个沉默的实验室，隐藏着自己的风险。

159
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:13,840
So what kind of reporting culture does your workspace really have?
那么，你的工作场所真正拥有的是怎样的报告文化呢？

160
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:16,320
Think about that the next time you step up to the bench.
下次你走到实验台前时，好好想一想这个问题。
